  ('c65fb3ad-568f-5c7f-8934-e3128729b4de', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-narrative-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The story is told in first person by a member of the stage crew. Which detail should NOT be added, because this narrator could not know it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Diego was secretly worried that he would forget his lines.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The audience grew quiet as Diego walked onto the stage.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-observable-detail"},{"text":"The tape felt sticky and cold against my fingers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-observable-detail"},{"text":"From across the stage, the director gave me a thumbs up.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-observable-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Diego was secretly worried that he would forget his lines.$q$, $q$A first-person narrator can report only what they see, hear, feel, or are told, so they cannot know Diego's secret worry. The other choices are things the narrator could hear, touch, or see from backstage.$q$, 'draft', '96f9060a-7370-599b-b872-d547316ed5a5')
